  "body": "## Problem\n\nPR #1689 moves the ortho near plane far behind the eye (about 20 x the view distance). The pick rays still start at the eye plane. A click through an opening can therefore pass over geometry that sits behind the eye plane and finds no hit.\n\n## Expected behaviour\n\nA pick in ortho mode finds the nearest hit along the ray from the near plane, not from the eye plane.\n\n## Notes\n\nFound during the delta review of PR #1689 (review comment https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/1689#pullrequestreview-5946226694). Non-blocking there. Small fix: start the ray at the near plane (or behind it) in the ortho branch of the pick path.\n",
